      {
        "id": "E2",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Detecting and recovering from silent data corruption on Amazon SageMaker HyperPod",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/detecting-and-recovering-from-silent-data-corruption-on-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T23:30:03.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:51.679Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Silent data corruption (SDC) happens when hardware, such as a GPU, returns a wrong but plausible number and raises no error.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/detecting-and-recovering-from-silent-data-corruption-on-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T23:30:03.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:51.679Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "It happens at scale: during a 54-day period of Llama 3 405B pre-training on up to 16K H100 GPUs, Meta attributed 6 of 419 unexpected job interruptions to silent data corruption, and those were only the cases that interrupted the job and were traced to SDC.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/detecting-and-recovering-from-silent-data-corruption-on-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T23:30:03.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:51.679Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Amazon SageMaker HyperPod already replaces nodes that report a fault: the health-monitoring agent watches for GPU errors, deep health checks stress-test nodes, and automatic node recovery swaps out bad hardware.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/detecting-and-recovering-from-silent-data-corruption-on-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T23:30:03.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:51.679Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "When a check fires, we map the suspect rank to its node, contain the corruption, and have SageMaker HyperPod replace the node.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/detecting-and-recovering-from-silent-data-corruption-on-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T23:30:03.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:51.679Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "We tested the checks with software-injected faults on a SageMaker HyperPod cluster with 4 ml.p5.48xlarge instances (32 NVIDIA H100 GPUs), and repeated every test on three instances, the minimum the checks need.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/detecting-and-recovering-from-silent-data-corruption-on-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T23:30:03.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:51.679Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Localize: On SageMaker HyperPod clusters orchestrated by Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS), the Kubernetes node name contains the instance ID, so mapping a suspect rank to a node is a lookup.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/detecting-and-recovering-from-silent-data-corruption-on-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T23:30:03.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:51.679Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Figure 1: A SageMaker HyperPod EKS cluster with three p5 nodes running training pods and SDC checks.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/detecting-and-recovering-from-silent-data-corruption-on-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T23:30:03.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:51.679Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Checkpoints on shared storage, Amazon FSx for Lustre or Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3).",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/detecting-and-recovering-from-silent-data-corruption-on-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T23:30:03.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:51.679Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "We ran the tests twice on one SageMaker HyperPod cluster orchestrated by Amazon EKS, using 4 and then 3 ml.p5.48xlarge instances with 8 NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3 GPUs each, and PyTorch 2.9.0 (CUDA 13.0) from the AWS Deep Learning Containers training image.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/detecting-and-recovering-from-silent-data-corruption-on-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T23:30:03.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:51.679Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E12",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "In this post, we showed how to detect silent data corruption in data-parallel training and how to hand a suspect node to SageMaker HyperPod for replacement.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/detecting-and-recovering-from-silent-data-corruption-on-amazon-sagemaker-hyperpod/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T23:30:03.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-13T17:42:51.679Z"
      }
